{"type":"text","timestamp":1790375840538,"sessionID":"ses_f2549c53dffei3WlKSa80ajMF9","part":{"id":"prt_0dab74b06001jRUTbiw200JfEQ","messageID":"msg_0dab700f4001zw7lLSP1yiVAEE","sessionID":"ses_f2549c53dffei3WlKSa80ajMF9","type":"text","text":"The main scene already assigns the `wizards` and `warlocks` groups. I’ll use a 32-pixel base range, giving the wizard’s range-4 stat a 128-pixel radius. I also found that `TargetFinder` becomes ready before the battle unit’s `onready` variables, so its signal connections will look up `DetectRange` directly.\n","time":{"start":1790375840518,"end":1790375840521},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_072aaaa2b7e05f4d016ab6f79e402087d19a493a80271f601c","phase":"commentary"}}}}
